OneiOS rt 0002: VK_KHR_surface and VK_KHR_swapchain are optional: Turnip on iOS is built with no window system (tu_wsi.h: no TU_USE_WSI_PLATFORM for platforms=macos) and the runtime calls neither; only a consumer's swapchain does.

diff --git a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/README.md b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/README.md
index f7bc4b6c2..72b5f2ab7 100644
--- a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/README.md
+++ b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/README.md
@@ -5484,8 +5484,8 @@ Presenting runs on the runtime's own device; nothing is exported or imported.
 
 | Extension | Where | Used for |
 |---|---|---|
-| `VK_KHR_surface` | instance | presenting |
-| `VK_KHR_swapchain` | device | presenting |
+| `VK_KHR_surface` | instance, where offered | presenting through a swapchain; a driver built with no window system (Turnip on iOS) offers neither it nor the swapchain, and the runtime calls neither |
+| `VK_KHR_swapchain` | device, where listed | presenting through a swapchain |
 | `VK_EXT_robustness2` | device | null descriptors, and image reads out of range answered by the device |
 | `VK_EXT_calibrated_timestamps` | device | GPU times on the host clock: the device calibrates its own clock (`VK_TIME_DOMAIN_DEVICE_EXT`) with the host's (`floor::TIME_DOMAINS`) |
 | `VK_EXT_line_rasterization` | device | lines drawn by Bresenham's rule, through `bresenhamLines` below; every venue's driver lists this name (RADV, ANV, lavapipe, NVIDIA's, KosmicKrisp, and the UHD 630's Windows driver, a Vulkan 1.3 device) |
diff --git a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/floor.rs b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/floor.rs
index 0e165934f..5fe2cc3cf 100644
--- a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/floor.rs
+++ b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/floor.rs
@@ -17,18 +17,22 @@ pub const VERSION: u32 = vk::API_VERSION_1_3;
 
 /// The instance extensions the runtime requires: presenting goes through a swapchain on the
 /// runtime's own device.
-pub const INSTANCE_EXTENSIONS: &[&CStr] = &[ash::khr::surface::NAME];
+pub const INSTANCE_EXTENSIONS: &[&CStr] = &[];
 
 /// The instance extensions instance creation enables where the loader offers them: the listing of
 /// portability devices, which the floor then checks as it checks any device.
-pub const OPTIONAL_INSTANCE_EXTENSIONS: &[&CStr] = &[ash::khr::portability_enumeration::NAME];
+pub const OPTIONAL_INSTANCE_EXTENSIONS: &[&CStr] = &[
+    ash::khr::portability_enumeration::NAME,
+    // Presenting: a driver built with no window system (Turnip on iOS) lists neither it nor the
+    // swapchain; the runtime calls neither, a consumer that presents through a swapchain does.
+    ash::khr::surface::NAME,
+];
 
 /// The device extensions the runtime requires and device creation enables: presenting, null
 /// descriptors and image reads out of range answered by the device, the GPU's clock read with
 /// the host's, for GPU times on the host clock ([`host_time`](crate::host_time)), and lines drawn
 /// by Bresenham's rule, Metal's (`VK_EXT_line_rasterization`'s `bresenhamLines`).
 pub const DEVICE_EXTENSIONS: &[&CStr] = &[
-    ash::khr::swapchain::NAME,
     ash::ext::robustness2::NAME,
     ash::ext::calibrated_timestamps::NAME,
     ash::ext::line_rasterization::NAME,
@@ -64,6 +68,8 @@ pub const TIME_DOMAINS: [vk::TimeDomainKHR; 2] =
 /// buffer access 2, and `VK_KHR_maintenance8` ([`MAINTENANCE8`]), for the
 /// optional feature of its own.
 pub const OPTIONAL_EXTENSIONS: &[&CStr] = &[
+    // Presenting, where the driver has a window system (see OPTIONAL_INSTANCE_EXTENSIONS).
+    ash::khr::swapchain::NAME,
     ash::khr::shader_maximal_reconvergence::NAME,
     ash::khr::shader_subgroup_uniform_control_flow::NAME,
     ash::khr::shader_quad_control::NAME,
